cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "University course timetabling with CP-SAT"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tkucukdeniz2/university-course-timetabling"
authors:
  - family-names: "Küçükdeniz"
    given-names: "Tarık"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6670-1809"
    affiliation: "İstanbul University-Cerrahpaşa, Department of Industrial Engineering"
abstract: >-
  A configurable curriculum-based course timetabling system built on Google OR-Tools
  CP-SAT. It schedules theory, application and lab blocks of undergraduate and
  graduate courses, assigns classrooms, a computer lab and faculty-granted
  amphitheatres, respects instructor availability and fixed faculty sessions, and
  maximises free days for students and instructors. Output is a formatted Excel
  workbook and a CSV file.
keywords:
  - course timetabling
  - constraint programming
  - CP-SAT
  - OR-Tools
  - scheduling
  - operations research
